  "result": "I've written the plan to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\add-a-new-parameter-delegated-book.md` but haven't changed any code yet. The tool for submitting a plan for approval isn't available here, so tell me when to start implementing.\n\n**How it will behave:**\n- I'll add a `KeyValue` class in `src/click/types.py`, right after the UUID type and built the same way. It splits the input on the first `=` and returns `(key, value)`.\n- Input with no `=` or an empty key fails with `'<input>' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- An empty value (`a=`) is accepted, and the value can contain `=` (`a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`).\n- If it receives a value that's already a tuple, such as a default, it returns it unchanged.\n- Help text shows the placeholder `KEY=VALUE`.\n- It works with `multiple=True`, so you can call `dict(...)` on the results.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- Export it from `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- Add a parametrized test in `tests/test_basic.py`, modeled on `test_uuid_option`.\n- Add entries in `docs/api.md` and `docs/parameter-types.md`.\n- `CHANGES.md` currently starts with 8.5.0, which is already released, so I'll add a new \"8.6.0 / Unreleased\" section for this.\n\nTo check it, I'll run `pytest tests/test_basic.py -k key_value`, then the full test suite.",
